      H("Early disseminated (weeks to months): multiple secondary annular lesions, cranial neuropathy - especially facial nerve palsy, which may be bilateral - lymphocytic meningitis, radiculopathy, and carditis with atrioventricular block."),
      H("Late (months to years): a monoarticular or oligoarticular arthritis, typically of the knee, with large effusions, and rarely a subtle encephalopathy or polyneuropathy."),
