      P("The HACEK organisms - Haemophilus species, Aggregatibacter, Cardiobacterium hominis, Eikenella corrodens, Kingella kingae - are fastidious oral Gram-negatives causing subacute endocarditis, historically 'culture-negative' because they grow slowly. Modern automated blood culture systems usually recover them within five days. Kingella is a notable cause of septic arthritis and osteomyelitis in toddlers."),
